 | Experiment | Decision / evidence |
 | --- | --- |
+| Draft-acceptance EMA memory 0.75 → 0.85 | Retained. Matched-input serving traces (fixed prompts, three bit-identical passes) show the width controller within ~8% of the per-request forced-width optimum on hard text and ahead of every fixed width on easy text; the loss concentrates in cooldown-retry storms (26% of rounds on hard/tools fixtures). The slower estimator damps those storms: 4v4 paired serving A/B gains +3.1/+1.7/+4.0/+2.0% on hard-story/easy-story/code/prose fixtures (every pair positive, CIs exclude zero, greedy outputs bit-identical across arms), one code sibling −0.8% (CI includes zero), sampled tools ~flat with one fixture +9%. Backoff to AR still arms within ~9 fully rejected cycles; controller unit tests updated to that contract. Evidence: strix-dual-exp `evidence/decode-tg/d1-stabilization`. |
 | Conversation checkpoints and asynchronous capture | Retained: edits, growing histories and rotation with bounded RAM; AR/MTP cancellation, image replay and disk restart pass, including four execution sessions. Intermediate copies allow peers to continue, and coincident RAM/disk boundaries share one copy. [Functional checks](../../../tests/functional/README.md). |
 | Prefix-independent MTP cache projections | Retained: exact seeded replay across prompt splits and checkpoint replacement, using shared Q8 row arithmetic. [Checks and timings](artifacts/mtp-cache-replay.json). |
 | Skip discarded MTP outputs | Retained: K/V-only prefill, compact catch-up and wider projection tiles; C1 costs remeasured. Prefill is within 0.3% of main; d0 TG remains 1.1% slower, d4K TG is 0.4% faster. |
@@ -46,6 +47,9 @@
 | Batched MTP catch-up tail | Retained; after writing every attention cache row, compact final request rows into existing scratch and skip unused output projections/FFNs. Preserve the scalar arithmetic of one-row tails; full-head candidates and recursive carry match independent execution. |
 | Routed Q8 accumulation order | Retained; explicit rounded product/FMA prevents identical rows changing with column placement. Independent FP64 dot and predictor carry checks pass. |
 | Isolated MMQ quantizer rounding change | Deferred: it changes half-integer tie behavior shared with W8A8 and fails their existing agreement gate. No quantizer change retained. |
+| Fused peer-add combine (TP2 paired prefill) | Retained. The paired lane's peer partial is acquired without adding and folded into the combine that consumes the local partial (`HcCombinePeerVec4Kernel`), replacing the separate `AddRowsBroadcast` pass; the summed row is written back only for the MoE observer, and an aliasing summed row (`block_summed == block_local`) is refused so the observer route keeps the separate add (without that guard the diagnostic path corrupted results: every MoE hash and a member checksum changed). Bit-exact against the unfused sequence (operator check at 37/2048 tokens; end-to-end member checksums and both-rank logit hashes unchanged). Kernel time: the 631 ms `AddRowsBroadcast` family disappears and the fused kernel runs 2 605 ms against the unfused pair's 2 826 ms at 32 k (~220 ms/rank). End-to-end: the paired probe's timed prefill was each process's first (±5 % cold noise), which produced unresolvable A/Bs; after adding an untimed warmup prefill (±0.7 % A/A), steady state is a median **+0.9 %** over a no-fusion twin — retained for the exact fused path and the removed pass, not a headline gain. |
+| Fixed-geometry (hidden 2,560) Vec4 combine specialization | Rejected: templating the hidden width constant-folds the stream/element index math (the ISA mix showed 41 % integer/select instructions) with the FP sequence bit-exact, but the fused peer kernel moved only −1.4 % per call (1 690 vs 1 714 µs in matched slow-mode profiles; expert-GEMM controls ±1–2 %) and end-to-end stayed within noise (2/3 pairs ≤ +1 %, single host even). The combine is latency/bandwidth-bound, not issue-bound. |
+| K/V-only draft catch-up in paired prefill | Retained. `ForwardPair`'s known-hidden catch-up forwards take the `kv_only` path the unpaired prefill already uses (persistent draft KV/indexer only; the next full forward rebuilds the predictor residual from kept trunk rows). Paired MTP prefill: median **+2.1 %** (four interleaved canary-gated pairs, +3.0/+1.2 % at 8 k, +1.5/+2.9 % at 32 k). Gates: paired `tp_probe --split` logits bit-identical; member tokens/checksums equal to the pre-change binary and to the greedy AR decode on both ranks; the chunk seam (4 104-token prompt) covered. |
 | SSM tile, wave and compiler scheduling variants | Rejected: four/sixteen-wave groups, wave64, wider token tiles and iterative ILP scheduling retained exact output but did not beat the existing eight-wave projection. |
 | SSM fragment lifetime and prefetch pipeline | Rejected: shorter-lived K16 fragments reduce register use without a useful gain; delayed prefetch and double-buffered LDS are slower. Projection/convolution outputs remain exact at 2048/2049 tokens. |
 | Captured shared stages in batched target decoding | Rejected: exact C2/C4/C6/C8 logits, sampled state and cancellation checks, but no serving or warmed-cycle gain justified graph metadata/capture overhead. |
@@ -65,6 +69,14 @@
 | GPU greedy penalties and linear CPU anchor selection | Retained; exact FP64 penalties, unchanged proposals and snapshots. Short heat-pump tg400: 32.12 → 33.80 tok/s; C2/4/6/8 improve 7.6/8.5/16.3/14.2%. Unpenalized control unchanged. [Evidence](artifacts/penalty-verification.json). |
 | Prefill projection, attention and indexer kernels | Retained; bit-identical logit dumps and greedy hashes, plus a bitwise GEMM sweep against hipBLASLt for every routed n ≤ 4096. pp4096 +1.4% at d0 and +2.5–2.8% at 32K/115K (interleaved ABBA, `-r 6`, two machines); repository prompts 6.5K–102K +3.2% median; tg unchanged. The indexer projections use the own kernel only when hipBLASLt selects algorithm 4438 and otherwise stay on the library. |
 | 128 n-gram readers | Rejected: first gather 179 → 140 ms, but no end-to-end change on repository prompts on two different NVMe drives (ABBA medians within 1%). |
+| KV cache 1-byte quantization pilot | Rejected as a default path and closed as performance-inconclusive. An env-gated measurement pilot quantized newly written trunk KV rows (int8 + FP16 scale per 32/16/8-element block, per-element E4M3, V-only and K+V; FP16 storage unchanged, draft cache untouched) and compared full-vocab logits over 428-row teacher-forced continuations: every format drifts to 78–92% top-1 agreement with mean KL 4e-3–5e-2 across synthetic and real 16k–38k histories, 5–10× the accepted TP2 reduction noise (98.4%, 0.0055). Speed: writer overhead ~0 (32k single-host prefill medians 1557/1550/1558 tok/s for FP16/v8/E4M3); the sparse attention family is largely DRAM-bound so packed halved-bytes caps at ~+3–4% prefill best case, ~+1–2% realistic after in-reader dequant, decode ≤0.75%. No native packed reader was built; the pilot code was removed. Evidence: strix-dual-exp `evidence/kv1-drift`. |
+| HC inject partials fused into the combine (TP2 + single host) | Retained. The F16-norm combine's plain and paired-peer routes also emit the next mixer's inject partials from the normalized values they already hold: the F16 norm row is staged in LDS (aliasing the peer kernel's dead block-row stage) and replayed with the separate pass's exact thread grouping, load order and reduction tree, so the emitted partials are byte-identical and `HcMix` skips its `HcMixEpilogueF16Kernel<false>` pass; separate sibling kernels keep the non-emitting route's codegen unchanged. Operator check exact at 37/2 048 tokens (plain, peer, emitted partials aliasing the consumed logits); single-host dump bit-identical; paired member checksums canonical in every session. The emitting combine costs ~1.7% per call; the separate inject pass halves single-host (376→184 calls at 8k, matched profiles, ≈+0.8% e2e, within session noise) and disappears on TP2. Canary-clean interleaved pairs @32k: **median +2.65% (4/4, full separation; 2 269→2 329 tok/s)**, 8k +2.3% (2/2), decode flat. The MoE-epilogue-fused combine keeps its separate pass: its norm compiles to mixed-precision `v_fma_mix*_f16`, which a source-level replay cannot reproduce bit-exactly. Evidence: strix-dual-exp `evidence/prefill-triage/hcf1`. |
